  "headline": "At gamma=4 the fused kernel moves 2.6x fewer bytes than the naive model yet runs 0.99x (on par with) the mx.compile'd reference. The roofline says memory-bound (arith intensity ~ 0.4-1.5 flop/byte vs ridge ~ 33), but a single-threadgroup kernel tops out at ~19% of peak bandwidth while MLX fans the op across every GPU core and hits ~48%: less traffic x worse occupancy = a wash. And the whole step is only ~2.3% of one target forward, and zero under greedy. mx.compile on the plain op graph is the right answer.",
